{
  "units": [
    {
      "id": "unit_1",
      "title": "Unit 1: Drawings",
      "lessons": [
        {
          "id": "u1_l1",
          "title": "Drawing types and scales",
          "theory": "In engineering, most design information is shown on **drawings**. Today, drawings are generally produced on computer using **CAD (computer-aided design)** systems.\n\nA key factor on a drawing is the **scale** - the size of items on the drawing in relation to their real size. When all items are shown relative to their real size, the drawing is a **scale drawing**. \n\n### Types of Drawings\n* **General arrangement (GA)**: Show whole devices or structures using a small scale (e.g., 1:100).\n* **Detail drawings**: Show parts in detail using a large scale (e.g., 1:5 or 1:2). Small parts are sometimes shown as **actual size** (1:1) or can be **enlarged** (e.g., 2:1).\n* **Schematic drawings (schematics)**: Simplified forms used for electrical circuits and pipe networks (e.g., a map of a train network).\n\nNote: 'Drawing' is often abbreviated to **dwg**.",
          "exercises": [
            {
              "type": "fill_in_the_blank",
              "question": "Enlarged drawings show components larger than their ____.",
              "blanks": [
                {
                  "position": 1,
                  "answer": "actual size"
                }
              ],
              "accepted_answers": [
                [
                  "actual size"
                ]
              ],
              "hint": "Refer to the size in real life.",
              "explanation": "Actual size (1:1) means the drawing is the same size as the real object. Enlarged means bigger."
            },
            {
              "type": "fill_in_the_blank",
              "question": "For engineering drawings, 1:5 is a commonly used ____.",
              "blanks": [
                {
                  "position": 1,
                  "answer": "scale"
                }
              ],
              "accepted_answers": [
                [
                  "scale"
                ]
              ],
              "hint": "It relates the drawing size to real size.",
              "explanation": "Scale determines how much an object is reduced or enlarged on paper."
            },
            {
              "type": "fill_in_the_blank",
              "question": "Whole machines or structures are shown on ____ drawings.",
              "blanks": [
                {
                  "position": 1,
                  "answer": "general arrangement"
                }
              ],
              "accepted_answers": [
                [
                  "general arrangement"
                ],
                [
                  "GA"
                ]
              ],
              "hint": "They show the overall assembly.",
              "explanation": "General arrangement (GA) drawings show the whole device or structure."
            },
            {
