        },
        {
          "id": "u1_l3",
          "title": "Drawing terminology in context",
          "theory": "In professional conversations, engineers use specific terms to describe the drawings they need or are reviewing. They might discuss the **scale**, ask for a **section** to see internal details, or refer to a **schematic** for simplified networks.",
          "exercises": [
            {
              "type": "fill_in_the_blank",
