        {
          "id": "u3_l2",
          "title": "Design calculations",
          "theory": "Engineers provide technical requirements in **specifications**. They must **determine** (identify) and **quantify** (calculate) the **loads** (forces) that components will carry. \n\nCalculations are usually based on a **worst-case scenario** (the maximum possible load). After quantifying these loads, engineers apply a **factor of safety** – an extra margin to ensure the component is strong enough.\n\n**Sizing** components means calculating their required dimensions. If an engineer adds excessive safety margins, they **overdesign** the component. This is sometimes called a **belt and braces** approach.",
          "exercises": [
            {
              "type": "fill_in_the_blank",
              "question": "The types of loads that will be encountered must be ____.",
              "blanks": [
