    {
      "id": "unit_4",
      "title": "Unit 4: Horizontal and vertical measurements",
      "lessons": [
        {
          "id": "u4_l1",
          "title": "Linear dimensions",
          "theory": "Engineers use specific terms for linear dimensions:\n\n* **Overall length**: Total measurement from front to rear (along a horizontal plane).\n* **Wingspan**: Total distance spanned by both wings.\n* **Overall height**: How tall an object is from the ground to the top (measured vertically).\n* **Width**: Measurement from side to side.\n* **Thickness**: The external or internal dimension of a wall or component.\n* **Span**: The distance between supports (e.g., in a bridge).\n\n**Planes** are imaginary surfaces shown as lines on drawings. They **strike** (touch) the faces (edges or surfaces) of components.",
          "exercises": [
            {
