    {
      "id": "unit_5",
      "title": "Unit 5: Locating and setting out",
      "lessons": [
        {
          "id": "u5_l1",
          "title": "Centrelines and offsets",
          "theory": "To locate points on components, engineers use **centrelines (CL)** – lines through the centre of holes or objects. Distances between centrelines are called **centre-to-centre (c/c)** dimensions. \n\nMeasurements are often **offset** from a centreline, meaning they are at a certain distance from it. Offsets are measured at a **right-angle** (90 degrees) to the centreline.",
          "exercises": [
