        {
          "id": "u5_l2",
          "title": "Grids and setting out",
          "theory": "In large designs, **grids** are used for horizontal positioning. **Gridlines** are numbered or lettered. Parallel gridlines are regular distances apart. **Perpendicular** lines run at right-angles to each other. \n\nGridlines **intersect** (cross) at the centres of columns. Site engineers **set out** (mark the position) of structures by **squaring off** gridlines – marking lines at right-angles using a **theodolite** (an optical device for measuring angles). To **double-check**, diagonal measurements are used.",
          "exercises": [
            {
              "type": "fill_in_the_blank",
