    {
      "id": "unit_6",
      "title": "Unit 6: Dimensions of circles",
      "lessons": [
        {
          "id": "u6_l1",
          "title": "Key dimensions of circles",
          "theory": "The geometry of circles is essential in engineering. Key terms include:\n\n* **Circumference**: The outside edge of a circle.\n* **Radius**: The distance from the centre to any point on the circumference. If it doesn't change, it is a **constant radius**.\n* **Diameter**: The distance across a circle through the centre (2 x radius).\n* **Arc**: A part of the circumference (a curved line).\n* **Chord**: A straight line between two points on a circle.\n* **Concentric circles**: Circles with different diameters that share the same centre.\n\nWhen a circular object like a tyre is compressed, it **deforms** (changes shape), changing an **arc** into a **chord**.",
          "exercises": [
            {
              "type": "fill_in_the_blank",
              "question": "The outer circle is perfectly ____.",
              "blanks": [
                {
                  "position": 1,
                  "answer": "circular"
                }
              ],
              "accepted_answers": [
                [
                  "circular"
                ]
              ],
              "hint": "Round.",
              "explanation": "A circle is circular in shape."
            },
            {
              "type": "fill_in_the_blank",
              "question": "Distance from centre to edge of tyre = ____.",
              "blanks": [
                {
                  "position": 1,
                  "answer": "radius"
                }
              ],
              "accepted_answers": [
                [
                  "radius"
                ]
              ],
              "hint": "Half the diameter.",
              "explanation": "Radius is the distance from the centre to the edge."
            },
            {
              "type": "fill_in_the_blank",
              "question": "Total distance across tyre = 2 x radius = ____ of tyre.",
              "blanks": [
                {
                  "position": 1,
                  "answer": "diameter"
                }
              ],
              "accepted_answers": [
                [
                  "diameter"
                ]
              ],
              "hint": "Full width through the centre.",
              "explanation": "Diameter is twice the radius."
            },
            {
              "type": "fill_in_the_blank",
              "question": "All points around the tyre are on the ____.",
              "blanks": [
                {
                  "position": 1,
                  "answer": "circumference"
                }
              ],
              "accepted_answers": [
                [
                  "circumference"
                ]
              ],
              "hint": "The outer edge.",
              "explanation": "Circumference is the perimeter of a circle."
            },
            {
              "type": "fill_in_the_blank",
              "question": "The tyre has a ____ radius.",
              "blanks": [
                {
                  "position": 1,
                  "answer": "constant"
                }
              ],
              "accepted_answers": [
                [
                  "constant"
                ]
              ],
              "hint": "It doesn't change.",
              "explanation": "Constant means staying the same."
