    {
      "id": "unit_7",
      "title": "Unit 7: Dimensional accuracy",
      "lessons": [
        {
          "id": "u7_l1",
          "title": "Precision and tolerance",
          "theory": "All production processes are **imprecise** to some extent. The sizes of components will **vary** (differ). They will not be 100% **accurate** (exact).\n\nEngineers specify **tolerances** – the acceptable **range** of sizes or allowed **variation**. This is often given as a **deviation** (difference) from a precise size (e.g., ±0.05 mm). \n\n* **Within tolerance**: A size that is **permissible** (allowed).\n* **Outside tolerance**: A size that is not allowed.\n* **Tight tolerance** (or **close tolerance**): A very small permissible deviation.\n* **Loose tolerance**: A large permissible deviation.",
          "exercises": [
            {
              "type": "fill_in_the_blank",
              "question": "Exact: ____",
              "blanks": [
                {
                  "position": 1,
                  "answer": "accurate"
                }
              ],
              "accepted_answers": [
                [
                  "accurate"
                ],
                [
                  "precise"
                ]
              ],
              "hint": "100% correct.",
              "explanation": "Accurate and precise both mean exact."
            },
            {
              "type": "fill_in_the_blank",
              "question": "Differ: ____",
              "blanks": [
                {
                  "position": 1,
                  "answer": "vary"
                }
              ],
              "accepted_answers": [
                [
                  "vary"
                ],
                [
                  "deviate"
                ]
              ],
              "hint": "To be different.",
              "explanation": "To vary or deviate means to differ from the intended size."
            },
            {
              "type": "fill_in_the_blank",
              "question": "Exactness: ____",
              "blanks": [
                {
                  "position": 1,
                  "answer": "precision"
                }
              ],
              "accepted_answers": [
                [
                  "precision"
                ],
                [
                  "accuracy"
                ]
              ],
              "hint": "The quality of being exact.",
              "explanation": "Precision is the level of exactness."
            },
            {
              "type": "fill_in_the_blank",
              "question": "Not exact: ____",
              "blanks": [
                {
                  "position": 1,
                  "answer": "imprecise"
                }
              ],
              "accepted_answers": [
                [
                  "imprecise"
                ],
                [
                  "inaccurate"
                ]
              ],
              "hint": "Opposite of precise.",
              "explanation": "Imprecise means not exact."
            },
            {
              "type": "fill_in_the_blank",
              "question": "Deviation between maximum and minimum: ____",
              "blanks": [
                {
                  "position": 1,
