              "explanation": "Loose tolerance is easier to achieve."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "u7_l2",
          "title": "Fit and mechanical play",
          "theory": "When components go together, their sizes must match. \n\n* **Clearance fit**: Leaves **clearance** (a gap) so parts can move or turn freely. \n* **Play**: The amount of movement allowed. Too much play is bad; **insufficient clearance** causes parts to **bind** (not move).\n* **Interference fit**: A very tight fit where parts don't move. Often achieved by heating (to **expand**) or cooling (to **contract**) parts before assembly.",
          "exercises": [
            {
              "type": "matching",
              "question": "Match the sentences about mechanical fit.",
              "pairs": [
                {
                  "term": "It'll bind",
                  "definition": "The bolt won't be able to turn freely enough"
                },
                {
                  "term": "It'll contract",
                  "definition": "The shaft will narrow slightly as it cools"
                },
                {
                  "term": "It'll expand",
                  "definition": "The hole will widen with high temperature"
                },
                {
                  "term": "Too much play",
                  "definition": "The bolt won't fit tightly enough"
                },
                {
                  "term": "Clearance fit",
                  "definition": "The bolt will have to turn in the hole"
                },
                {
                  "term": "Interference fit",
                  "definition": "The wheel will have to fit very tightly"
                }
              ],
              "hint": "Think about expansion, contraction, and movement.",
              "explanation": "These terms describe how parts interact when assembled."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "u7_l3",
          "title": "Engine blueprinting",
          "theory": "Engine blueprinting involves building an engine to extremely precise specifications by matching parts that are within a specific range of the overall tolerance.",
          "exercises": [
            {
