    {
      "id": "unit_8",
      "title": "Unit 8: Numbers and calculations",
      "lessons": [
        {
          "id": "u8_l1",
          "title": "Decimals and fractions",
          "theory": "In engineering, numbers are expressed as **decimals** (e.g., 0.04) or **fractions** (e.g., 1/100). \n\n* **Whole numbers**: Numbers like 1, 2, 3 (not decimals).\n* **Rounding**: Decimals are often **rounded up** or **rounded down** to a certain number of **decimal places**.\n* **Rounding error**: A small error caused by rounding that can add up in calculations.\n* **Negligible**: A difference so small it doesn't matter.",
          "exercises": [
