          "title": "Elements, compounds and mixtures",
          "theory": "Materials have different chemical compositions:\n\n* **Elements**: Pure materials in their basic form (e.g., iron, carbon).\n* **Compounds**: Elements chemically bound by a reaction (e.g., water - H₂O).\n* **Mixtures / Alloys**: Elements or compounds mixed together but not chemically bound. **Alloys** are metals mixed with other elements (e.g., steel is an iron-carbon alloy).",
