          "id": "u12_l2",
          "title": "Corrosion",
          "theory": "Corrosion is a chemical reaction between iron and oxygen (O₂) to form **iron oxide** (**rust**).\n\n* **Rusting**: Specifically refers to the corrosion of iron-based metals.\n* **Oxidation**: The reaction with oxygen.\n* **Passive layer**: Metals like aluminium form a hard oxide layer that prevents further corrosion. Mild steel, however, flakes off, allowing corrosion to continue.",
