          "id": "u13_l1",
          "title": "Common non-ferrous metals",
          "theory": "Non-ferrous metals do not contain iron:\n\n* **Aluminium**: Lightweight, often alloyed with titanium or copper. **Duralumin** contains aluminium, copper (4.4%) and magnesium (1.5%).\n* **Copper**: Excellent electrical conductor, ductile (used for wires and pipes). Alloys: **Brass** (copper + zinc) and **Bronze** (copper + tin + lead).\n* **Titanium**: High strength-to-weight ratio; used in aerospace.\n* **Precious metals**: High-cost metals. **Silver** is the best electrical conductor. **Gold** is an excellent conductor and highly corrosion-resistant.",
