        {
          "id": "u13_l2",
          "title": "Plating and anodizing",
          "theory": "Non-ferrous metals can protect steel from corrosion by **plating** it:\n\n* **Galvanizing**: Coating steel with zinc (hot-dip or electro-galvanized).\n* **Electroplating**: Depositing metal via electric current. \n    * The component is the **cathode** (-).\n    * The plating metal (e.g. zinc) is the **anode** (+).\n    * The bath contains an **electrolyte** liquid.\n* **Anodizing**: Protecting aluminium by depositing a hard oxide layer on the component (functioning as the anode).",
          "exercises": [
            {
              "type": "fill_in_the_blank",
              "question": "In electroplating, the component is the (1) ____ and the plating metal is the (2) ____. Zinc plating is called (3) ____.",
