    {
      "id": "unit_16",
      "title": "Unit 16: Concrete",
      "lessons": [
        {
          "id": "u16_l1",
          "title": "Concrete mix design",
          "theory": "Concrete is a mixture of **cement**, **fine aggregate** (sand), **coarse aggregate** (gravel), and water. \n\n* **Set**: When concrete begins to become solid.\n* **28-day strength**: The point where concrete reaches its structural strength.\n* **Batching**: Measuring precise quantities of ingredients by weight.\n* **Water-cement ratio**: The amount of water relative to cement; excess water reduces strength.\n* **Additives**: Chemicals like **plasticizers** (to help flow) or **retarders** (to delay setting).",
          "exercises": [
