        {
          "id": "u16_l2",
          "title": "Reinforced and prestressed concrete",
          "theory": "Concrete is weak in **tension** (stretching), so steel **reinforcement** bars are added.\n\n* **Formwork** / **Shuttering**: Moulds used to contain wet concrete until it sets.\n* **In-situ**: Concrete cast in its final position.\n* **Precast**: Concrete elements cast at a factory and then delivered.\n* **Prestressing**: Applying tension to reinforcing bars before (**pre-tensioning**) or after (**post-tensioning**) pouring to increase resistance to bending.",
          "exercises": [
            {
              "type": "multiple_choice",
              "question": "Why is steel used in reinforced concrete?",
