          "id": "u17_l1",
          "title": "Categories of wood",
          "theory": "Wood is divided into two biological categories:\n\n* **Hardwood**: From deciduous trees (e.g., oak).\n* **Softwood**: From coniferous trees (e.g., pine).\n\nEngineering formats:\n\n* **Solid wood**: Sawn timber with natural grain and knots.\n* **Engineered wood**: Made by bonding layers or particles with resin (e.g., plywood, OSB, glulam).",
