          "title": "Structural timber and engineered wood",
          "theory": "Structural timber is tested to determine its **stress grade**:\n\n* **Rough-sawn**: Surface texture from circular saws.\n* **Planed**: Smoothed surface for visibility.\n* **Stress-grading**: Mechanical (by machine) or visual (by inspector).\n* **Glulams**: Glue-laminated sections used for large structural beams.\n* **Plywood**: Layers (**plies**) bonded with grain at 90 degrees.",
