    {
      "id": "unit_21",
      "title": "Unit 21: Material formats",
      "lessons": [
        {
          "id": "u21_l1",
          "title": "Raw materials and basic blocks",
          "theory": "Raw materials often require processing before use (e.g., melting/casting). Common formats:\n\n* **Powder**: Very fine particles (e.g., cement).\n* **Pellets**: Standard pea-to-egg sized pieces (e.g., plastic).\n* **Fibres**: Hair-like lengths (e.g., glass fibres).\n* **Ingots**: Large blocks of metal produced at foundries.\n* **Blooms**: Very large steel ingots.\n* **Billets**: Smaller blocks of steel.",
          "exercises": [
