    {
      "id": "unit_26",
      "title": "Unit 26: Mechanical fasteners 1",
      "lessons": [
        {
          "id": "u26_l1",
          "title": "Bolts and nuts",
          "theory": "Common fasteners include bolts and nuts:\n\n* **Threaded shaft** (**shank**): The part of the bolt with grooves.\n* **Nut**: Screwed onto the bolt by a turning motion (usually clockwise).\n* **Socket head**: A hexagonal hole in the bolt head for a **hex key** (**Allen key**).\n* **Spanner** / **Wrench**: Tools used to turn hexagonal heads.",
          "exercises": [
            {
              "type": "matching",
              "question": "Match the fastener with its tool:",
              "pairs": [
                {
