        },
        {
          "id": "u26_l2",
          "title": "Torque and washers",
          "theory": "Managing force in joints:\n\n* **Torque**: The turning force applied to a bolt.\n* **Preload** (**clamp load**): The pressing force that holds components together.\n* **Work loose**: When a joint becomes loose over time due to vibration.\n* **Washers**:\n    * **Plain washers**: Spread the load over a wider area.\n    * **Spring washers**: Compressed to allow preload adjustment or absorb shocks.",
          "exercises": [
            {
              "type": "fill_in_the_blank",
              "question": "(1) ____ washers spread the load; (2) ____ washers absorb shocks. The turning force is (3) ____.",
              "blanks": [
                {
                  "position": 1,
                  "answer": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "position": 2,
                  "answer": "Spring"
                },
                {
                  "position": 3,
                  "answer": "torque"
                }
              ],
              "accepted_answers": [
                [
                  "Plain",
                  "Spring",
                  "torque"
                ]
              ],
              "explanation": "Washers protect surfaces and maintain joint tension."
            },
            {
              "type": "fill_in_the_blank",
              "question": "Pressing force is (1) ____. If it becomes loose due to vibration, it (2) ____ loose. Excess force causes (3) ____.",
              "blanks": [
                {
                  "position": 1,
                  "answer": "preload"
                },
                {
                  "position": 2,
                  "answer": "works"
                },
                {
                  "position": 3,
                  "answer": "tension"
                }
              ],
              "accepted_answers": [
                [
                  "preload",
                  "works",
                  "tension"
                ]
              ],
              "explanation": "Textbook 26.2 verification."
            },
            {
              "type": "multiple_choice",
              "question": "Which washer is used to absorb shocks?",
              "options": [
                {
                  "text": "Plain washer",
                  "is_correct": false
                },
