              "explanation": "The solvent evaporates to leave the bond."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "unit_37",
      "title": "Unit 37: Fluid containment",
      "lessons": [
        {
          "id": "u37_l1",
          "title": "Pipes, ducts and hoses",
          "theory": "Transporting liquids and gases:\n\n* **Pipes**: Rigid tubes for fluids; a network is called **pipework**.\n* **Ducts**: Tubes for air not under pressure (HVAC).\n* **Hoses**: Flexible tubes (**fuel lines**, **air lines**).\n* **Mains**: Underground pipes for water or gas supply.\n* **Pipeline**: Long-distance transport (e.g., for oil).",
          "exercises": [
            {
              "type": "fill_in_the_blank",
              "question": "Long distance transport: (1) ____. Water/gas supply: (2) ____. Waste water: (3) ____. Underground street waste: (4) ____.",
