        {
          "id": "u39_l2",
          "title": "Flow and aerofoils",
          "theory": "Controlling air movement:\n\n* **Laminar flow**: Smooth, direct path.\n* **Turbulent flow**: Disturbed, messy path.\n* **Aerofoil**: Component shaped to generate force (e.g., **wing**, **propeller blade**).\n* **Forces**: **Lift** (upward), **Thrust** (forward), **Downforce** (downward).\n* **Pitch** (**Angle of attack**): Angle relative to the airflow.",
