      "lessons": [
        {
          "id": "u42_l1",
          "title": "Chains and pulleys",
          "theory": "Flexible transmission:\n\n* **Roller chain**: Transmits drive across a distance to **sprockets**.\n* **Belt drive**: Uses a belt and **pulley wheels** (**sheaves**).\n* **Slip**: When a belt slides around a pulley; **toothed belts** prevent this.\n* **Mechanical advantage**: Achieved using combinations of pulleys (e.g., in cranes).",
          "exercises": [
            {
              "type": "matching",
              "question": "Match the transmission part:",
