          "id": "u43_l2",
          "title": "Voltage, resistance and power",
          "theory": "Managing electricity:\n\n* **Voltage**: Electromotive force (EMF) measured in **Volts**.\n* **Resistance**: How easily current flows, measured in **Ohms** (Ω).\n* **Insulator**: Material with high resistance (e.g., plastic).\n* **Ohm's Law**: Current (I) = Voltage (E) / Resistance (R).\n* **Power**: Measured in **Watts** (W). Power (P) = Voltage x Current.",
